---
// Half-fare and property tax bus passes (#955, part of #393): Mountain
// Line's Gold Card, Medicare and disability, and Property Tax Bus Pass
// programs, from their PDF forms and program pages. Every fact is quoted in
// content/pdf-pages/mountain-line-passes.yaml.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import FromPdf from '../components/FromPdf.astro';
import { pdfPage } from '../lib/pdf-pages.mjs';
export const page = { door: "living-here", topic: "moving", label: "Half-fare and property tax bus passes", summary: "Mountain Line's Gold Card for ages 62 and up, half fare with Medicare or a disability, and the Property Tax Bus Pass: who can get each and how to apply" };
const d = pdfPage('mountain-line-passes');
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Base title="Half-fare and property tax bus passes in Morgantown: Mountain Line" description="Mountain Line's bus pass programs in Morgantown and Mon County: the Gold Card for riders 62 and older, half fare for Medicare cardholders and people with disabilities, and the Property Tax Bus Pass, with who qualifies, the cost and how to apply.">
  <h1>Half-fare and property tax bus passes</h1>
  <p class="lede">Mountain Line has passes that make the bus cheaper or free for some riders. Each one uses a form that is a PDF. Here is what the forms and Mountain Line's pages say, in short lists.</p>

  <nav aria-label="On this page">
    <ul>
      {d.sections.map((s) => <li><a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.heading}</a></li>)}
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <FromPdf d={d} />

  <p>Regular fares, free rides with a WVU ID and the Grey Line are on <a href={`${base}/getting-around/`}>Getting around without a car</a>. Every route and its hours are on <a href={`${base}/bus-routes/`}>Every bus route and when it runs</a>.</p>

  <p class="meta">This page is a reading aid. Mountain Line decides who gets a pass. Something wrong? <a href="https://github.com/david-shortman/mon-county-community-hub/issues/new?template=suggest-resource.yml">Tell us what is wrong on this page</a>.</p>
</Base>
